WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.069
Throughout 2018, there were plenty of major
blockbusters and indie films alike that were

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:08.340
big hits with audiences despite being panned
by critics.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:11.400
Don't let the negative reviews discourage
you from checking them out.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:16.020
Here are a few films that deserve a second
look, contrary to the critical consensus.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:22.020
The character Venom first appeared on the
big screen in 2007's Spider-Man 3, but 2018's

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:25.240
Venom gives viewers a new origin story for
the famous anti-hero.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:30.140
When Eddie Brock, played by Tom Hardy, tries
to investigate the Life Foundation for running

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:35.200
dangerous human trials, he ends up accidentally
bonding with an alien slime and developing

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.480
strange powers.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.480
Even though Venom has been criticized for
everything from its dialogue to its plot to

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:44.300
its cinematography, it's a fun, campy film
that stands on its own.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:48.760
The technical details might be clunky, and
the visuals might seem cliche, but it's the

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:52.080
kind of train wreck that you won't feel guilty
about sticking around to watch.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:53.180
"I have proof!"

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.539
The Nun is the fifth installment in The Conjuring
franchise, and turned out to be the highest-grossing

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:06.820
entry since the original.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:11.330
Although fans of the series flocked to theaters
to see it, critics didn't exactly hold it

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:12.240
in high esteem.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:17.140
The Nun was dismissed by some critics as a
series of jump scares and other horror tropes.

00:01:17.149 --> 00:01:21.920
Still, there's a lot to like in the film,
notably Taissa Farmiga, and fans will find

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:25.750
that it's a welcome addition to the franchise
with familiar themes on the struggle between

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:26.740
good and evil.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:27.740
"We need to pray, now.

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:33.500
And whatever happens, whatever you may see
or hear, keep your eyes forward and don't

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:34.420
stop praying."

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:38.940
The Spy Who Dumped Me is a refreshing action
flick with a heavy dose of female empowerment.

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:44.060
After Audrey is unceremoniously dumped by
her boyfriend via text message, she discovers

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:47.780
that he's secretly a CIA agent… and now,
he's gone missing.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:51.680
It's up to Audrey and her best friend Morgan
to figure out what's happened to him and come

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:52.560
to the rescue.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:57.340
Most of the criticism of The Spy Who Dumped
Me focused on the film's refusal to pin itself

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:58.740
to one single genre.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.719
Still, there's nothing wrong with a little
creative genre blending, and ultimately it

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.360
all comes together for a solidly entertaining
film.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:07.960
"This is how people get shoved into the back
of sketchy vans, right?"

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:11.840
"That actually makes this awkward."

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:14.480
"Get in the van."

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:16.760
Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes of Grindelwald

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.870
Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes of Grindelwald
brings Eddie Redmayne back to the big screen

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:20.000
as Newt Scamander.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:24.440
Unfortunately, this new installment in the
Fantastic Beasts franchise struggled as far

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:25.620
as the critics were concerned.

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:30.540
In the film, Newt joins forces with Albus
Dumbledore as they race to stop the infamous

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:34.480
dark wizard Grindelwald from establishing
a worldwide wizard supremacy.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:38.950
The Crimes of Grindelwald has been criticized
for packing in too many plot twists and tiny

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:43.140
details for the audience to keep track of,
and putting the actual exciting magic on the

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:43.740
back burner.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:47.730
Still, there's something to be said for a
film that demands your close attention throughout

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.880
if you want to fully grasp the storyline.

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:55.440
In Tully, Charlize Theron plays Marlo, a stressed,
sleep-deprived mother of two with another

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.480
baby on the way.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:01.689
When her brother offers to pay for a night
nanny to lessen her load, she eventually accepts.

00:03:01.689 --> 00:03:05.660
The new nanny's name is Tully, and she brings
a new energy to Marlo's life.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:10.480
While some critics felt that Theron's performance
was the only winning note in this film, Tully's

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:14.689
strength lies in the fact that it shows a
realistic side of modern motherhood that most

00:03:14.689 --> 00:03:16.240
movies are hesitant to touch on.

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:21.720
Marlo might be exhausted and overworked, but
she refuses to lose her own identity in motherhood.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:22.760
"Are you okay?"

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:23.260
"Oh.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:23.900
Yeah.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:29.040
That's milk.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:30.560
I make milk."

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:35.740
Rampage stars Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson as
a primatologist who has to stop three giant

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:39.100
rampaging monsters: a gorilla, a wolf, and
a crocodile.

00:03:39.629 --> 00:03:44.260
As far as sci-fi monster movies go, Rampage
really isn't half bad, taking the video game

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:46.300
premise into action movie territory.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:49.380
What could be more fun than watching The Rock
fight giant monsters?

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:54.260
Although Vulture called the film "aggressively
dumb," director Brad Peyton clearly knew what

00:03:54.269 --> 00:03:58.629
his target audience wanted: Rampage was nominated
for several Teen Choice Awards.

00:03:59.629 --> 00:04:03.790
The Meg follows a group of scientists, one
of whom is played by the incomparable Jason

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:08.160
Statham, who unexpectedly run into a megalodon
shark in the depths of the Pacific Ocean.

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:12.660
The Meg isn't going for realism, but it's
got plenty of moments that will make you laugh,

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:14.040
and a few that will make you shudder.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:19.060
The film might have been criticized as "neither
good enough nor bad enough" by Variety, but

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:22.880
that didn't stop plenty of eager viewers from
flooding the cinema to see it.

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:26.640
The Meg hits that sweet spot somewhere between
Jaws and Sharknado.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:28.700
“Aw yeah, jellyfish."

